# docs/calibration/X3-PROVISIONAL.log — @pixagram/paph-x 1.2.0
#
# X3-PROVISIONAL — X2's schedule, bars, route derivation and door, bound to CAL-007-PROVISIONAL —
# beside X2-PROVISIONAL (bound to CAL-004, --x2), on the corpora hashed in wire 4
# (CAL-007-PROVISIONAL.log, runs 1-2); and wire 4's evidence: the route's global words, the SI cells
# and the DCT section on every D4 copy, in both formats. Quoted by docs/PAPH-X.md (header, §2, §4's
# 1.2.0 subsection, §5, §6), docs/SPEC-W4-paph-wire4.md §6 and §10, docs/SPEC-SI-paph-si.md §9.8 and §11,
# docs/SEARCH.md, docs/PERFORMANCE.md, the README and the CHANGELOG.
# Native, one core of a shared two-core container (Intel(R) Xeon(R) Processor @ 2.10GHz), rustc 1.97.0;
# rust/target/release/{sibench,xbench,xcli}, run from rust/; Node 22.22 for the test/ and tools/ scripts,
# run from the repository root. Counts, classes, recalls and artefacts are deterministic and reproduce
# exactly from the same snapshot; timings move by a few per cent between runs, and more when the host is
# busy.
#
# The snapshot is 1.1.2's (docs/calibration/SI3-PROVISIONAL.log, run 0): rust/target/chain-corpus,
# head block 987642, manifest sha256 8d06cb4711e0e1e9c43dabe50edf3ed11039975a17dbc9bfec0afcf1dd27c055.
# The images are not in the repository; no author or permlink appears in the output.
#
# The wire-3 runs read 1.1.2's caches kept beside the new ones: chain-w3.bin is 1.1.2's chain.bin
# (sha256 c2985634154c9686…, as SI3-PROVISIONAL.log records), corpus-w3.bin the synthetic corpus
# hashed in wire 3 (82a6de6706583d40…); `sibench corpus [--chain target/chain-corpus] --wire 3
# --out NAME` writes each again byte for byte, and `load` notes their format. Under --x2 the SI
# cells are SI2's (the profile bound to X2 for the synthetic corpus); SI3's on the chain's wire-3
# hashes are in SI3-PROVISIONAL.log.
#
# The first pass of these runs found a defect in the cascade (docs/PAPH-X.md §4, "The fix the
# measurement found"): `sibench lost` read two synthetic copy queries NotCopy under X3. Every run
# below is on the fixed engine. rust/bench.sh and test/bench-engines.mjs time hashing in both
# formats. Then the pair behind the fix, through `xcli` (`sibench dump` writes its wires; fast and
# safe policy under copy scope, both orders, X3 and X2), and the ties the silhouette's component
# choice can meet on free polyominoes (`tools/silhouette-ties.cjs`, docs/SPEC-W4-paph-wire4.md §6);
# the last run prints the unit tests' result lines.

